-- title:
--   The halving-search counter is bounded by its search cap
-- statement:
--   Let $q\in\mathbb Q$ and let $\operatorname{den}(q)$ be its positive reduced denominator. The bounded halving search starts with counter $0$ and value $1$, repeatedly increments the counter and halves the value while the current value exceeds $q$, and permits at most $\lfloor\log_2\operatorname{den}(q)\rfloor+8$ iterations. Its returned counter $b$ satisfies $$b\le\lfloor\log_2\operatorname{den}(q)\rfloor+8.$$
-- source:
